{
 "_note": [
  "Hand-written, human-reviewed part-of-speech labels: {language: {data-pos-key: term}}.",
  "Keys are DDO's own data-pos-key values (s20_parse.KNOWN_POS_KEYS), never the 41",
  "mangled display strings the 2025 pipeline translated (guide 1.11f). This table is",
  "what makes an offline .apkg possible: without it G-COV blocks every export until a",
  "paid Gemini POS call has run. Stage 42 still translates keys that are MISSING here,",
  "so a brand-new target language needs no registry edit -- and an unknown pos_key",
  "(the vocabulary is open: 'formelt subjekt' was in nobody's list) fails G-COV loudly",
  "instead of shipping an unlabelled group. translations/<lang>/pos.json overrides a",
  "row here; work/registry/pos_translations.json overlays it per language.",
  "Terms are standard grammatical vocabulary in each language: German capitalises its",
  "nouns, Chinese uses the school-grammar terms with no pinyin.",
  "Two keys name the same thing: the 2026 corpus serves `infinitivpartikel`, while",
  "`infinitivens` is an older data-pos-key spelling that is still in",
  "s20_parse.KNOWN_POS_KEYS and has zero hits in the current corpus. Both rows are",
  "kept and carry the same term in each language, so whichever spelling DDO emits",
  "renders identically and neither can force a paid POS call. The other rows the",
  "2026 corpus does not use are kept for that same reason: a legal KNOWN_POS_KEYS",
  "value with no row here is a paid call waiting to happen."
 ],
